## Project Structure and Entry Points

- Backend entry point: [fastapi_backend/main.py](mdc:fastapi_backend/main.py)
- Backend configuration: [fastapi_backend/core/config.py](mdc:fastapi_backend/core/config.py)
- Backend routers live in [fastapi_backend/api/](mdc:fastapi_backend/api/)
- Backend models live in [fastapi_backend/models/](mdc:fastapi_backend/models/)
- Database connection: [fastapi_backend/database/connection.py](mdc:fastapi_backend/database/connection.py)
- Alembic migration env: [fastapi_backend/alembic/env.py](mdc:fastapi_backend/alembic/env.py)

- Frontend entry point: [frontend/src/main.jsx](mdc:frontend/src/main.jsx)
- Frontend app root: [frontend/src/App.jsx](mdc:frontend/src/App.jsx)
- Frontend components: [frontend/src/components/](mdc:frontend/src/components/)
- Frontend pages: [frontend/src/pages/](mdc:frontend/src/pages/)
- Frontend API layer: [frontend/src/api/](mdc:frontend/src/api/)

## Modular Domains

- Authentication & Users: [fastapi_backend/api/auth.py](mdc:fastapi_backend/api/auth.py), [fastapi_backend/models/user.py](mdc:fastapi_backend/models/user.py)
- Files & Uploads: [fastapi_backend/api/files.py](mdc:fastapi_backend/api/files.py), [fastapi_backend/services/file_service.py](mdc:fastapi_backend/services/file_service.py)
- Notifications & Messaging: [fastapi_backend/api/notifications.py](mdc:fastapi_backend/api/notifications.py), [fastapi_backend/api/messaging.py](mdc:fastapi_backend/api/messaging.py)

## Single Responsibility and File Size Limits

- Each file should express a single responsibility and remain small:
  - Backend Python files: hard limit 300 lines, target ≤ 200 lines.
  - Frontend component/page files: hard limit 200 lines, target ≤ 150 lines.
  - Break out helpers into modules under `lib/`, `hooks/`, or `services/`.

## Naming and Locations

- Place new API endpoints in a dedicated router file under `fastapi_backend/api/`.
- Place business logic in service modules under `fastapi_backend/services/`.
- Place new React components under `frontend/src/components/` and pages under `frontend/src/pages/`.
